      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The shogi pawn moves one square straight forward, and it also takes straight forward, unlike a chess pawn. It never moves two squares at once. It comes from shogi, Japanese chess, where it promotes to move like a gold general once it reaches the far three ranks, and where any captured piece joins the side that took it and can be dropped back onto the board. This app plays neither rule: here it never promotes, and on the last rank it can't move at all. The marked square is the only one it can reach.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "s": "shogiPawn" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3S4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the shogi pawn to the marked square. It takes two moves.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "s": "shogiPawn" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/8/3S4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["d6"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The shogi pawn is one of the weakest pieces there is. It is worth less than a chess pawn, because here it can't promote. Its job is to take squares from the enemy one step at a time.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "s": "shogiPawn" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3S4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A shogi pawn guards only the square in front of it. Two shogi pawns side by side don't protect each other, as chess pawns do, so keep a piece behind them. Here the king backs up the pawn.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "s": "shogiPawn" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3S4/3K4/8/8 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A piece diagonally in front of a shogi pawn is safe from it. Here the black bishop attacks the pawn from e5, and the pawn can't take it back. It can only step forward, out of the attack.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "s": "shogiPawn" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/4b3/3S4/8/8/7K w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "d5"]]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
